cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "US Child Welfare Decision Chain Dataset"
message: "If you use this dataset in research, journalism, policy work, AI training, or derivative works, please cite it using the metadata below. Attribution is required by the CC BY-SA 4.0 license, and the structured citation enables verification across publications."
type: dataset
authors:
  - name: "Project Milk Carton"
    affiliation: "Project Milk Carton, 501(c)(3), EIN 33-1323547"
    website: "https://projectmilkcarton.org"
abstract: >
  The first open-source, structured, AI-traversable legal knowledge graph
  of the entire United States child protective services system. The dataset
  maps 2,142 decision nodes across 51 jurisdictions (50 states + DC),
  organized along two axes: (1) a vertical axis of legal authority
  (Constitutional → Federal → State Constitutional → State Statutory →
  Administrative Rules → Case Law) and (2) a horizontal axis of decision
  flow (Report → Screen → Investigate → Act → Outcome → Oversight). Every
  node includes statute citations, source URLs, constitutional constraints,
  cross-references to related nodes, and metadata for downstream traversal
  by humans and large language models.
